title: '4. How hard a plan is read is set by signs anyone can count: the planner counts them, Tay may raise the tier but not lower it, and Top only looks it up.'
pid: 7e712327-58f6-46c1-afc7-0ab909b7c33f
body: |2-
  The signs: one-way doors; territories changed and borders crossed;
  building missions, and builders other than the author's specialist;
  questions for Jeff that Tay cannot answer. The tiers:
  - Tay: one territory, one building mission by the author's own specialist, no one-way door.
  - Tay, then Libby: a border crossed, more than one building mission, or another builder.
  - Tay, Libby and Jeff: any one-way door, or a question Tay cannot answer.
  Why, and its sources: [[id:f73e6a70-70f3-47e4-b6ae-388b1b973915][step 4, its reasons]].
